From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Thu, 18 Jun 2026 11:30:34 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 02562/11362] [outer-loop] curious/directed exploration:
 first-contact solves jump 1->3 (sp80, cn04, ar25)

Replaces random exploration with CURIOUS/DIRECTED exploration: BFS over the reachable AGENT-POSITION
graph (dedup on the agent's centroid, not the full grid), trying every action at each newly-reached
position until a level-up. For navigation/movement games the agent position is the state variable
that matters, so covering reachable positions is ~O(#positions) instead of the exponential
O(branching^depth) of random walks -- it reaches deep wins random play cannot stumble.

RESULT (results/arc3_test_time_goal_induction.json, fully first-contact, NO banked solve):
  sp80: solved  4 actions (random already could)
  cn04: solved 14 actions  <-- random FAILED to stumble; curious cracked it (banked solve is 13)
  ar25: solved 15 actions  <-- random FAILED to stumble; curious cracked it (incl its reflect win)
  ka59: win still NOT stumbled -- push mechanic: the win depends on the PUSHED object's position,
        not just the agent's, so agent-position coverage misses it (an honest, specific limit).

First-contact solves jumped 1/4 -> 3/4. The full unseen-game pipeline -- explore -> identify agent
-> induce goal object -> plan(best_first_search) -> solve -- now works end to end on 3 distinct
games with ZERO prior knowledge. Remaining limit localized: push/multi-object games need the state
key to include the pushed object's position (agent-position-only coverage is insufficient there).
Adversarial-verify: clean.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
